<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eleanor of Aquitaine</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1122–1204</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eleanor of Aquitaine was Duchess of Aquitaine and Countess of Poitou in her own right from 1137. She was queen of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> as wife of Louis VII, and after the annulment of that marriage she married Henry of Anjou in 1152, bringing Aquitaine into the Angevin Empire. She was the mother of the English kings <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-i-of-england">Richard I</a> and John.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/eleanor-of-aquitaine.jpg" alt="Eleanor of Aquitaine" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Adam Bishop · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Church_of_Fontevraud_Abbey_Eleanor_of_Aquitaine_effigy.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
